Traffic, Energy and Environment Tax Act |\n| ㉔ Matters for reference | |\n\nI apply for approval for tax-exempt release pursuant to Article 16, subparagraph (____), of the Traffic, Energy and Environment Tax Act.\n\nYear ____ Month ____ Day ____\nApplicant: ____________________ (Signature or seal)\n\nTo the Head of the Tax Office / Customs Office\n\nNo. ______\n\nThe matters stated in the above application are approved.\n\nYear ____ Month ____ Day ____\nHead of the Tax Office / Customs Office: ____________________ [Seal]\n\nTo: ____________________\n\nRequired documents: See reverse.\n※ This application form is distributed free of charge.\nFee: None.\n\nGeneral paper, 60 g/m² (recycled), or newsprint, 54 g/m² (recycled)\n\n(Reverse)\n\nRequired Documents\n\nCategory: Unconditional exemption\n\n1. In the cases under Article 16, subparagraphs 1 and 4, of the Traffic, Energy and Environment Tax Act: Documents issued by the head of the competent ministry certifying the relevant facts.\n2. In the case under Article 16, subparagraph 2, of that Act: Documents required for an application for exemption under the Customs Act.\n3. In the case under Article 16, subparagraph 3, of that Act: Documents issued by the head of the government institution or local government receiving the articles as a donation certifying receipt of the donation.\n4. In the cases under Article 16, subparagraphs 5 and 6, of that Act: Documents issued by the head of the competent tax office certifying the relevant facts.\n\nThis application is processed as follows.\n\n<table>\n<tr><th>Applicant</th><th>Processing authority: Head of the tax office / customs office having jurisdiction over the place of business</th></tr>\n<tr><td>1. Prepare application</td><td>2. Receive application (Civil Service Office)</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>3. Investigate and verify (Department in charge)</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4. Decide (Final decision delegated to the department head)</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>5. Prepare 